{"series":{"id":"intestine-program-center-state::intestine-program-waitlist-end-2025","label":"Intestine waitlist registrations at year end · center state","dataset_id":"frozen-atlas","unit":"program waiting-list registrations at December 31, 2025","scope":"us_states","definition":"Program waiting-list registrations at December 31, 2025, summed over reporting intestine programs by center state. A person listed at several programs can appear more than once. This is a year-end stock, not annual new candidates and not unique people across programs.","denominator":"None; absolute program counts, not resident-population rates or risk-adjusted outcomes.","reporting_period":"Calendar 2025; SRTR PSR released July 7, 2026","source_url":"https://srtr.hrsa.gov/Archives/PSRdownloads/csrs_tables/csrs_final_tables_2605_IN.xls","sources":[{"id":"srtr-intestine-psr","title":"SRTR July 2026 national program-specific tables · Intestine","url":"https://srtr.hrsa.gov/Archives/PSRdownloads/csrs_tables/csrs_final_tables_2605_IN.xls","date":"Released July 7, 2026; selected calendar 2025","note":"Tables use programs, not resident states. Table B1 NC2 is the 2025 interval; recipient field RCC_N_C is the program patient count. Original XLS, converted XLSX and a current Georgetown PDF cross-check retained.","license":"SRTR states material is not copyrighted and may be used without permission with appropriate citation: https://srtr.hrsa.gov/requesting-data/citations-and-permissions/"},{"id":"srtr-psr-methods","title":"SRTR July 2026 PSR technical methods","url":"https://srtr.hrsa.gov/transplant-professionals/program-specific-report/technical-methods-for-the-program-specific-reports/","date":"Reports released July 7, 2026; OPTN data available April 30, 2026","note":"Defines program counts, Table B1 yearly intervals, repeat listings and table suppression when no patients. Some residual date wording remains on the methods page; actual July 2026 Georgetown PDF confirms the 2025 periods.","license":"SRTR material may be used with appropriate citation."},{"id":"optn-center-code-convention","title":"OPTN center-code state convention · official briefing paper footnote 6","url":"https://www.hrsa.gov/sites/default/files/hrsa/optn/20200115_hi_pr_briefing_paper.pdf","date":"January 15, 2020; stable identifier convention","note":"Documents that the first two letters of transplant center codes identify the state or territory. Used only for center-location grouping, never patient residence.","license":"Public U.S. government/OPTN document; attribution retained."}],"limitations":["These SRTR maps group reporting programs by center state, not donor, candidate or recipient residence. People may travel across states. They are distinct from the HRSA residence-based topic.","The public Table B1 roster contains 17 intestine programs in 12 states/DC jurisdictions. The recipient table has 15 program rows. States with a missing roster-program table/value remain null; states without a program row remain null, not zero.","New registrations count repeat additions and can count one person at multiple programs. Year-end registrations are a separate stock. Do not interpret program sums as unique statewide people.","Recipient counts are for deceased-donor intestine programs and can involve multi-organ transplantation. They are not organ-recovery totals, all-organ procedure counts, resident counts or a measure of donor authorization.","SRTR publishes some program counts smaller than HRSA disclosure thresholds. Source-specific published counts are retained; unavailable tables are not imputed. No SRTR count is used to fill a suppressed HRSA cell.","Absolute program counts do not describe population need, individual eligibility, wait time, success probability or center quality. Small counts and program coverage limit comparisons.","Calendar 2025 is the selected common year. A July 2026 release date is not a 2026 activity year."],"interval_type":null,"display_reference":null,"years":[2025],